    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) commands our highest efficiency score as he faces Bieber, benefiting from an elite matchup against a starter with an xERA of 5.25 and a favorable park factor. Close behind, **Drake Baldwin** (67.49) continues his strong run at the top of the order; his leadoff role combined with a plus-matchup against Pfaadt makes him a cornerstone of today's lineup. We are also leaning heavily into our outfield depth, where **Kyle Tucker** (65.04) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (64.28) provide massive ceilings. **Luis Robert Jr.** specifically gains a significant platoon edge against the southpaw Alvarez, though we are tracking a slight penalty due to the opposing catcher's efficiency at mitigating stolen base attempts, which remains a focal point for our strategy.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Jackson Merrill** (50.99), who narrowly missed the cut. While his underlying metrics are solid, he faces a stiff test against Williams and his 2.90 xERA; the optimizer favored the higher park-adjusted projections of **Heliot Ramos** and **Nasim Nunez** in their respective matchups against weaker arms. Meanwhile, we are monitoring the slow delivery of Matz, which provides a small but meaningful boost for **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** in their pursuit of stolen bases, even as both face platoon challenges. With **Jordan Westburg** sidelined on the IL and **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Luis Lara**, **Sam Antonacci**, and **Miguel Vargas** providing additional depth, we are comfortable with our current configuration, provided that the lineup spots for **Drake Baldwin** and **Wade Meckler** hold firm as projected.",
